{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dizzy-muscovite-drever","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_commands cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mcp_client.py:1-33` — Preserve the two actionable client-wiring failure classes. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py:1-44` — Preserve diagnostic-versus-repair boundary and non-destructive guarantees. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py:1-28, 101-107` — Preserve per-environment tally purpose and identity-divergence data. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py:1-19, 44-109, 313-317, 604-740` — Preserve orphan classification, incomplete-log refusal, dry-run, and human-triage boundaries. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_restore.py:25-34, 61-96, 130-196` — Preserve newest-deletion selection, per-path fallback, retired-file restoration, and incomplete-log refusal. Consumer: test coverage asserts the related recovery documentation retains `get_rotation.json`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py:1-21, 56-93, 128-176, 261-267, 319-412` — Preserve check ownership,